WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.134
Evidence is the bridge between control claims and assessment conclusions.

00:00:04.134 --> 00:00:07.764
For a High-impact service, unsupported assertions are not enough.

00:00:07.764 --> 00:00:13.008
The cloud service provider needs evidence that reflects the real system: policies, procedures,

00:00:13.008 --> 00:00:16.234
diagrams, implementation descriptions, configuration records, logs, tickets, scans,

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:19.865
test results, operational records, security monitoring outputs, incident records,

00:00:19.865 --> 00:00:21.882
risk decisions, and remediation tracking.

00:00:21.882 --> 00:00:28.335
The cloud service provider implements and operates the service and prepares evidence that accurately describes it.

00:00:28.335 --> 00:00:30.755
A 3PAO, at a high level,

00:00:30.755 --> 00:00:34.386
performs independent assessment work and produces evidence-based assessment results.

00:00:34.386 --> 00:00:38.823
Agency reviewers and authorizing officials use the package, findings, risk information,

00:00:38.823 --> 00:00:42.050
and mission context to support a risk decision.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.663
These roles are distinct,

00:00:43.663 --> 00:00:48.100
and the relationship works best when evidence is clear and timely.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.327
High assessment requires strong consistency between documentation, implementation,

00:00:51.327 --> 00:00:52.134
and operations.

00:00:52.134 --> 00:00:54.150
Diagrams should match deployed architecture.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.974
Procedures should match ticket and log patterns.

00:00:56.974 --> 00:01:00.604
Control statements should match tool configurations and operational records.

00:01:00.604 --> 00:01:03.024
If the evidence does not align,

00:01:03.024 --> 00:01:07.058
reviewers may not be able to trust the control story.

00:01:07.058 --> 00:01:11.898
Consistency is a sign that security is being operated, not merely described.

00:01:11.898 --> 00:01:17.142
Findings and remediation plans should be treated as part of mature risk management.

00:01:17.142 --> 00:01:21.176
The goal is not to pretend that no weaknesses exist.

00:01:21.176 --> 00:01:26.016
The goal is to identify issues, assign ownership, track milestones, evaluate risk,

00:01:26.016 --> 00:01:27.226
and remediate effectively.

00:01:27.226 --> 00:01:28.839
In a High-impact context,

00:01:28.839 --> 00:01:33.680
the quality of the remediation process matters because unresolved or poorly tracked

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.100
weaknesses can carry serious mission consequences.
